WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.075
Here's how assessment usually works.

2
00:00:02.075 --> 00:00:05.600
The network team reviews the
boundary, keyed by address.

3
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:10.600
The cloud team runs each provider's
posture scan, keyed by resource tags.

4
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:14.075
The virtualization team
works a hypervisor checklist.

5
00:00:14.075 --> 00:00:17.504
At year end someone puts
the three reports behind one

6
00:00:17.504 --> 00:00:21.088
cover page and calls it the
agency's Zero Trust maturity.

7
00:00:21.088 --> 00:00:23.824
It's three partial
assessments with one title.

8
00:00:23.824 --> 00:00:27.125
The failure is architectural,
not organizational.

9
00:00:27.125 --> 00:00:29.723
A policy decision can only treat a user,

10
00:00:29.723 --> 00:00:35.325
a device and a resource consistently if
every platform describes them the same way.

11
00:00:35.325 --> 00:00:40.600
One database server can show up as three
unrelated objects, scored by three tools.

12
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:44.000
A total across them counts
objects, not architecture.

13
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.513
The federal guidance describes
the enterprise, not a tenant.

14
00:00:47.513 --> 00:00:51.303
Executive Order 14028, M-22-09,

15
00:00:51.303 --> 00:00:56.825
CISA's maturity model and NIST
all speak in agency-wide terms.

16
00:00:56.825 --> 00:01:01.550
A scan can confirm that an architecture
is unified; it can't make it unified.

17
00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:06.637
So the first decision: reconcile the
network, every cloud and the virtualization

18
00:01:06.637 --> 00:01:11.800
estate to one authoritative asset and
identity record before scoring any of them.

19
00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:16.375
The book gives that to the owner of the
naming and identity plane, this quarter.

20
00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:18.990
Until it's done, report any whole-agency

21
00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:22.013
figure as partial
assessments, not one score.

22
00:01:22.013 --> 00:01:26.090
Next, why this is a security
issue, not a reporting preference.
